  "body_html": "<h1>Nash Equilibria Are Rationalizable</h1>\n<p>If $s$ is a Nash equilibrium, then $s$ is rationalizable.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>Sketch</p>\n<p>The singleton set $\\{s\\}$ satisfies\n$$\n  \\{s\\}\\subseteq BR(\\{s\\})\n$$\nbecause every component of $s$ is a best response to the other components. Since\n$S^\\infty$ is the largest set $L$ with $L\\subseteq BR(L)$, it contains $\\{s\\}$.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Cor. 4.5.4] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>. Every Nash equilibrium is rationalizable.</li>\n</ul>",
